  "rationale": "obs[S1]: AllMusic credits and review list a core band of Freddie Hubbard, Richard Wyands, George Benson, Ron Carter, Jack DeJohnette, Airto Moreira, and Phil Kraus, plus a woodwind/string ensemble arranged by Don Sebesky, and tag the album Post-Bop / Soul Jazz / Jazz-Funk / Fusion. obs[S2]: Wikipedia confirms the CTI release, producer Creed Taylor, Van Gelder Studio sessions, and notes it won the 1972 Grammy for Best Jazz Performance by a Group. obs[S4]: The CTI sessionography gives exact recording dates (September 14 and 16, 1971), per-track session mapping, and session-level personnel. inf: The album fits the canon window as a high-profile, Grammy-winning CTI record that bridges hard-bop trumpet with orchestrated soul-jazz/post-bop production.",
