    "notes": "Two sessions at Van Gelder Studio, Englewood Cliffs, NJ: September 14, 1971 (track 2 'Uncle Albert/Admiral Halsey') and September 16, 1971 (tracks 1, 3, 4, 5, 6). CTI S4 marks the September 16 tracks as 'same or similar' to the September 14 collective personnel. Unresolved conflicts: (1) Richard Wyands' instrument: CTI S4 specifies electric piano (el-p), while AllMusic S1 review says 'acoustic piano' and its credits list 'Piano', and Wikipedia S2 lists 'piano'. (2) Herbie Hancock and Eric Gale are credited as performers in AllMusic S1 review and Wikipedia S2 lead, but they do not appear in the CTI S4 sessionography or the Wikipedia S2 formal Personnel section; they are recorded as disputed entries with epistemic=unk. (3) Track durations differ between AllMusic S1 / Wikipedia S2 / Discogs S3 (e.g., 'Yesterday's Dreams' 3:55) and the CTI S4 sessionography (4:55). (4) Freddie Hubbard's CTI S4 credit is 'tp on d, flhrn' \u2014 trumpet on 'Yesterday's Dreams' and flugelhorn on the other five tracks. (5) Taxonomy gaps: 'bassoon' (Jane Taylor, Wally Kane doubling) and 'conductor' (Don Sebesky) are not in the current instrument taxonomy. A live 1973 bonus performance of 'First Light' appears on reissues but is excluded from the original album tracks."
